{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VUHkNXrZmWx243uCtQnpii","type":"tool_result","content":"The JUnit reporter writes to a file by default, not to stdout. Per the Reporter Output section, the `junit` reporter \"instead write[s] to a scoped location under `.vitest/`\", and the JUnit section says: \"By default it is written to `.vitest/junit/output.xml`.\"\n\nTo change the location, you can use the top-level `outputFile` option or the reporter's own `outputFile` option. To print to the terminal instead, set the reporter's `stdout` option. The docs note that `stdout` is ignored when `outputFile` is set."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b2f0dbd-e881-442a-9e19-dbe86708c395","uuid":"ba3887b1-f5be-4a7f-b11b-cacbf8d6c246","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:15:55.458Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":212241,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The JUnit reporter writes to a file by default, not to stdout. Per the Reporter Output section, the `junit` reporter \"instead write[s] to a scoped location under `.vitest/`\", and the JUnit section says: \"By default it is written to `.vitest/junit/output.xml`.\"\n\nTo change the location, you can use the top-level `outputFile` option or the reporter's own `outputFile` option. To print to the terminal instead, set the reporter's `stdout` option. The docs note that `stdout` is ignored when `outputFile` is set.","durationMs":3765,"url":"https://vitest.dev/guide/reporters"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VUHkNXrZmWx243uCtQnpii","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
